    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαγγ-έλλω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ελῶ</span>: aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διήγγειλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					1.6.2
				</span></i>
			:—<i>give notice by a messenger,</i> c. dat.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.73
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i> l.c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. εἰς . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					3.11.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span> Philipp. ap.
				<i><span class="en">
				D.
				12.16
			</span></i>: generally, <i>noise abroad, proclaim,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ὅτι . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					5.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				436
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				317a
			</span></i>: c. inf., <i>order</i> to do, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				353
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>pass</i> the word of command <i>from man to man,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.4.36
			</span></i>.</div>
